      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any particular reason to use a version number, apart from templates using version numbers?\nInstead of managing another version number that ultimately maps to the set of fields that are supported, you could use another uint32_t that represents the bitmask of supported features (supported fields).\nThe flashprotect command may already do something similar.\n\nJust an idea if you weren\u0027t already married to the version number approach.",
