      "writtenOn": "2019-06-03T17:19:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason to use uint16_t struct_version is to be consistent with other struct formats we are using. It\u0027s not a solid reason.\n\nFor the bitmask approach I am not sure if at some point we would want to change the format of \"status\" (the \"status\" itself is a bitmask) like removing or reordering some status bits? If it\u0027s just adding status bits then the bitmask approach you mentioned would be clearer than a version number.",
